---
import DocShell from '../../layouts/doc-shell.astro';
import { docsLinks } from '../../lib/nav';

const toc = [
   { id: 'build', label: 'Build a report' },
   { id: 'outputs', label: 'Outputs' },
   { id: 'publication', label: 'Publication and recovery' },
];
---

<DocShell
   title="a1 report build"
   summary="Combine a discovery inventory and per-page audit results into HTML, PDF, JSON, and one W3C EARL report."
   links={docsLinks}
   toc={toc}
>
   <section class="panel" id="build">
      <h2>Build a report</h2>
      <pre><code>a1 report build \
   --inventory .a11ied/audits/createdbyfireside-com/inventory.json \
   --results-dir .a11ied/audits/createdbyfireside-com/pages \
   --out .a11ied/audits/createdbyfireside-com/report</code></pre>
      <p>
         Use <code>--formats html,json</code> to skip PDF and EARL when a fast local check is
         enough. JSON is always written because it is the complete presentation data contract.
         <code>--fail-on</code> uses the same impact levels as <code>a1 audit</code>.
         Exit code 4 reports findings at that threshold after the bundle has been written;
         it does not mean file generation failed.
      </p>
      <p>
         Add <code>--draft</code> to view an unfinished assessment in one command. It reads
         available page results, labels HTML and PDF as drafts, and sets
         <code>status: "draft"</code> in JSON. Page statuses and the saved inventory stay
         unchanged. Pending checks remain incomplete; the command does not perform them.
      </p>
      <pre><code>a1 report build \
   --inventory .a11ied/audits/createdbyfireside-com/inventory.json \
   --results-dir .a11ied/audits/createdbyfireside-com/pages \
   --out .a11ied/audits/createdbyfireside-com/preview --draft</code></pre>
   </section>

   <section class="panel" id="outputs">
      <h2>Outputs</h2>
      <div class="route-list">
         <div class="route-row"><code>report.html</code><span>Self-contained report for a browser.</span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><code>report.pdf</code><span>Print-ready copy of the HTML report.</span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><code>report.json</code><span>Every fact shown by the built-in report.</span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><code>report.earl.json</code><span>One EARL JSON-LD graph for all audited pages.</span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><code>report.manifest.json</code><span>Generated file paths, SHA-256 hashes, formats, and assessment revision when supplied.</span></div>
      </div>
      <p>
         Without <code>--draft</code>, every selected page must have valid audit results with no pending procedures, or
         an explicit error with a reason. Missing or corrupt files for pages marked audited
         block generation. In a sampled audit, unselected pages stay not tested and do not
         block the report. The report includes recorded manual evidence and coverage gaps.
      </p>
   </section>
   <section class="panel" id="publication">
      <h2>Publication and recovery</h2>
      <p>
         Report files are rendered in a sibling staging directory and checked against the
         manifest before the complete directory replaces the published bundle. A rendering
         failure preserves the previous report. Concurrent builds for the same output
         directory run one at a time.
      </p>
      <p>
         After an interruption, repeat the same command. It discards unfinished generation
         or recovers a verified directory swap before building again. Unexpected directory
         replacements stop recovery and preserve their files. A swap can leave the output
         directory temporarily absent until recovery finishes.
      </p>
      <p>
         Use a dedicated output directory outside the inventory, page results, run file,
         verified raw evidence inputs, and the current working directory. Existing unrelated
         files and old artifact files are retained. Unselected report formats are removed
         from the new bundle. PDF artifact links point to the published local bundle directory.
      </p>
      <p>
         Successful publication confirms that the generated files passed their hash checks.
         Assessment completion remains a separate value in the manifest and report.
      </p>
   </section>
</DocShell>
